          "dataType": "value",
          "angle": 90
        },
        {
          "id": "left",
          "label": "left",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "value",
          "angle": 180
        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "question-driven-explanation-template"
        },
        "markdown": "# Reading This Idea\n\nThe graph argues for a reusable explanation template rather than implementing the template itself. Follow the semantic edges from the problem with undifferentiated documents toward a small question-and-answer grammar.\n\nThe central design choice is deliberate: **Who, What, Where, When, Why, and How are seeded instances of one `qa-question` class with a `lens` field**, not six separate node classes.",
        "title": "Reading This Idea"
      }
    },
